# UI/UX Design Standards (React Native Mobile)

## Visual Design
- Establish a clear visual hierarchy to guide user attention
- Use `constants/colors.ts` for a cohesive palette — never hardcode colors
- Use typography effectively (Clash Display for headings, Satoshi for body) via `constants/fonts.ts`
- Maintain sufficient contrast for legibility (WCAG 2.1 AA: 4.5:1 for text)
- Design with a consistent style across the application

## Interaction Design
- Create intuitive navigation (Expo Router, bottom tabs, clear back/continue flows)
- Use familiar UI components (chips, buttons, cards) to reduce cognitive load
- Provide clear calls-to-action (Continue, Skip, Done) to guide user behavior
- Use `useWindowDimensions` / `Dimensions.get` for responsive layouts
- Use animations judiciously (`react-native-reanimated`) to enhance UX

## Accessibility (React Native)
- Add `accessibilityLabel` and `accessibilityRole` to interactive elements
- Provide `accessibilityHint` for non-obvious actions
- Ensure touch targets are at least 44x44 pt (minWidth/minHeight)
- Support Dynamic Type / system font scaling where applicable
- Test with TalkBack (Android) and VoiceOver (iOS)

## Performance
- Use `expo-image` for images (lazy loading, optimized formats)
- Implement lazy loading for non-critical content
- Memoize lists with `FlatList`; use `keyExtractor` and avoid inline functions
- Monitor render performance; avoid unnecessary re-renders

## User Feedback
- Use `ActivityIndicator` for async operations (loading states)
- Provide clear error messages and recovery options (retry buttons)
- Disable buttons during submit (`disabled={loading}`)
- Use haptic feedback for meaningful interactions when appropriate

## Information Architecture
- Organize content logically (onboarding steps, tab structure)
- Use clear labeling and categorization for navigation
- Implement effective search when applicable (explore tab)
- Maintain consistent placement of recurring elements (back top-left, continue bottom)

## Mobile-First Design
- Design for mobile devices first (SwipTurn is mobile app)
- Use touch-friendly targets: min 44x44 pt for buttons, chips, icons
- Implement gestures for common actions (swipe cards on swipe tab)
- Consider thumb zones for primary actions (bottom tabs, continue button)

## Consistency
- Adhere to `constants/colors.ts` and `constants/fonts.ts`
- Use consistent terminology (Continue, Skip, Done, Saved)
- Maintain consistent positioning (header back left, step indicator center)
- Ensure visual consistency across onboarding, tabs, auth

## Layout and Responsiveness
- Use Flexbox for all layouts (React Native default)
- Use `useSafeAreaInsets` for safe areas — never hardcode padding
- Use `useWindowDimensions` when layout must adapt to screen size
- Test on multiple device sizes and orientations

## Touch Targets
- Interactive elements: min 44x44 pt (buttons, back, icons)
- Adequate spacing (gap 8–16) between adjacent touch targets
- Use `Pressable` with `hitSlop` when needed for small icons

## Forms
- Use `KeyboardAvoidingView` for forms with multiple fields
- Use appropriate `keyboardType` for inputs (email, numeric)
- Implement inline validation and clear error messaging
- Use `ScrollView` so keyboard does not obscure content

## Testing
- Test on actual devices, not just simulators
- Verify touch target sizes and spacing
- Test with accessibility features enabled
- Conduct usability testing across device types

